categories based on the distribution of the main active sites.[48-52] The first category is the combination of MOFs and conductive carbon materials, where the MOFs are the main active species towards ORR while carbon materials serve as the vastly conductive network. For instance, Jahan et al. reported a hybrid of pyridine-functionalized graphene with iron-porphyrin MOF composite for ORR.[48] As shown in Figure 4A, the composite (denoted as (G-dye-FeP)n MOF) was formed by combination of G-dye and (Fe-P)n MOF, where G-dye represents reduced graphene oxide (rGO) functionalized with donor- $\cdot\pi\cdot$ - acceptor dye, and (Fe-P)n MOF represents a MOF created by linking FeCl3 and 5,10,15,20-tetrakis(4- carboxyl)- $\cdot21H,23H.$ -porphyrin (TCPP). By optimizing the structure-composition relationship, the composite with $50\mathrm{wt}\%$ of G-dye manifested the best catalytic performance with an Eonset of $0.93{\mathrm{~V~}}$ vs RHE and a jL of $-6.3\mathrm{\mA}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ (Figure 4B). In a most recent study by Zhong et al., they reported a Cuphthalocyanine-based 2D conjugated MOF (PcCu-O8-Co) with square planar cobalt-bis(dihydroxy) complexes as linkages (Figure 4C).[53] The introduction of carbon nanotubes (CNTs) into MOFs forms the composite of PcCu-O8-Co/CNTs with the uniform mixture of layered MOFs and CNTs (Figure 4D). The high coverage of active sites and good conductivity as well as the porous structure jointly render the PcCu-O8-Co/CNTs composite a 3.93-electron pathway for ORR in alkaline media. Both of the half-wave potential (E1/2, 0.83 V vs RHE) and jL $(5.3\mathrm{\mA\cm^{-2}},$ ) are the record values reported for pristine MOF electrocatalysts (Figure 4E).
The second category is the combination of MOFs with metal or metallic compounds, where the metal or metallic compounds are the active species and MOFs function as support or reaction chamber.[45,54] He et al. reported a bifunctional electrocatalyst based on MIL-101-Cr (MIL $\c=$ Material from Institut Lavoisier) and cobalt.[55] The as-prepared Co/MIL-100-Cr with higher $\mathrm{Co^{II}}$ contents showed better ORR activity. Cho et al. used thioacetamide to partially vulcanize a MOF of HKUST-1 $\mathrm{\Delta[Cu_{3}(B T C)_{2}{\cdot}(H_{2}O)_{3}]}$ to prepare a series of nano-CuS $(\mathrm{~x~}\mathrm{wt}\%$ ) $@$ HKUST-1 (x stands for the amount of
